<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<%= render partial: 'shared/assets' %>
<body class="bg-gray-dark color-white">
<div class="w-100">
	<%= render partial: 'shared/menu', locals: {active: "home", appearance: "light"} %>
</div>
<div class="jumbotron jumbotron-fluid mb-4">
	<div class="container">
		<h1 class="heading text-uppercase">Readersourcing</h1>
		<h2 class="text-uppercase">Crowdsourcing in Scholarly Peer Review</h2>
		<h3>An independent, third-party, nonprofit academic project dedicated to assessing the quality of scholarly literature and scholars.</h3>
	</div>
</div>
<div id="home-page" class="container">
	<div class="row">
		<div class="col-lg-6 col-xs-12 mt-4">
			<div class="heading text-center">
				<h1>Rate a publication</h1>
			</div>
			<p class="lead text-justify mb-2">
				Enter the URL of the PDF publication you want to evaluate, then assign it a score from 0 to 100.<br>
				If you have not finished reading it, you can annotate the PDF with a link that allows you to submit your rating later.<br>
				The weight of your rating depends on your reader score, which in turn reflects your ability to evaluate publications accurately (more details).<br>
				You can also choose to rate anonymously; in that case, your reader score will not change.<br>
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="col-lg-6 col-xs-12 mt-4 text-center">
			<img class="img-fluid" src="<%= asset_path("rating-section.png") %>" alt="Rating Section">
		</div>
	</div>
	<div class="row">
		<div class="col-lg-6 col-xs-12 mt-4 text-center">
			<img class="img-fluid" src="<%= asset_path("publication-table.png") %>" alt="Publication Table">
		</div>
		<div class="col-lg-6 col-xs-12 mt-4">
			<div class="heading text-center">
				<h1>Browse ratings</h1>
			</div>
			<p class="lead text-justify mb-2">
				Browse the list of publications that have already received at least one rating. You can download an annotated PDF and rate
				the publication, contributing to its final score.<br> You can also browse the list of readers, view their scores, and download the annotated
				PDFs of the publications they have rated.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
	<div class="row">
		<div class="col-lg-6 col-xs-12 mt-4">
			<div class="heading text-center">
				<h1>Install the browser extension</h1>
			</div>
			<p class="lead text-justify mb-2">
				If you install the Chrome extension of Readersourcing, you can evaluate publications directly from your browser.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="col-lg-6 col-xs-12 mt-4 mb-2 text-center">
			<a href="https://chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/readersourcing-20-rsrate/hlkdlngpijhdkbdlhmgeemffaoacjagg?hl=it" target="_blank">
				<img class="img-fluid" alt="Available on Chrome Webstore" src="<%= image_path("chrome-webstore-badge.png") %>">
			</a>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
<%= render partial: "shared/footer" %>
</body>
</html>
